   "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Oxidation of Met-44 and Met-47 by MICALs (MICAL1, MICAL2 or MICAL3) to form methionine sulfoxide promotes actin filament depolymerization. MICAL1 and MICAL2 produce the (R)-S-oxide form. The (R)-S-oxide form is reverted by MSRB1 and MSRB2, which promote actin repolymerization (By similarity)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "PTM"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "value": "Monomethylation at Lys-84 (K84me1) regulates actin-myosin interaction and actomyosin-dependent processes. Demethylation by ALKBH4 is required for maintaining actomyosin dynamics supporting normal cleavage furrow ingression during cytokinesis and cell migration"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "PTM"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Belongs to the actin family"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "SIMILARITY"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Could be the product of a pseudogene"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "CAUTION"
  }
